id: rust.graceful-shutdown
kind: rust
title: Graceful shutdown in Tokio
aliases: graceful shutdown, SIGTERM, drain
tags: shutdown, resilience, operations
questions:
  - how does your service shut down without dropping requests?
invariant: On shutdown: stop accepting, cancel background work, drain in-flight requests under a deadline, then exit.
answer_30s: Catch SIGTERM, stop accepting new work, let in-flight requests finish within a bounded timeout, signal workers to drain, then exit before the platform kills the process.
answer_2m: |
  The ordering is the content: stop accepting (no new work), cancel the loops
  and workers, await in-flight tasks with a bounded timeout, exit. In Kubernetes
  the deadline is terminationGracePeriodSeconds, and the Pod is removed from
  endpoints slightly after SIGTERM is delivered -- which is why clients need
  retries and why a small preStop delay or a readiness flip is worth having.
  Workers follow the same protocol: stop pulling, finish the current item,
  acknowledge it, exit. Anything that cannot finish is abandoned explicitly, and
  must be either idempotent or requeued.
when_to_use:
  - every long-running service and worker
minimal_example: |
  use tokio_util::sync::CancellationToken;

  let cancel = CancellationToken::new();
  let signal = cancel.clone();
  tokio::spawn(async move {
      tokio::signal::ctrl_c().await.ok();
      signal.cancel();
  });

  axum::serve(listener, app)
      .with_graceful_shutdown(async move { cancel.cancelled().await })
      .await?;
failure_modes:
  - no drain, so every deploy drops in-flight requests
  - an unbounded drain, so the orchestrator SIGKILLs the process mid-write
  - workers that stop pulling but never acknowledge what they held, so messages are redelivered later
follow_ups:
  - what is the interaction with readiness probes during shutdown?
related:
  - rust.cancellation
  - rust.tokio-select
  - design.graceful-shutdown
  - k8s.deployment.rolling-update
  - recipe.graceful-shutdown
sources:
  - https://docs.rs/axum/latest/axum/serve/struct.Serve.html
